    {
      "block": "library/10665-44759/blocks/prose-sec-006",
      "source": "sections/sec-006-31-use-of-igras-in-diagnosis-of-active-tb.md",
      "source_hash": "618ad148cb9f21a9de9ff25a27a8147ed31a410c4bae2dead625abd33630c8a6",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "A section heading for the use of IGRAs in diagnosing active TB.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44759/blocks/prose-sec-007",
      "source": "sections/sec-007-311-study-characteristics.md",
      "source_hash": "2f65ab2db386a5c2dc8b22d993b0854c943ce9ec50fb199743f41d7696b776cb",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes the studies included on IGRAs for diagnosing active pulmonary TB in adults in low- and middle-income countries, limited to the two current commercial assays. It explains how sensitivity and specificity were estimated, the latter only among suspects found not to have active TB.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44759/blocks/prose-sec-008",
      "source": "sections/sec-008-312-summary-of-results.md",
      "source_hash": "910616a7f4fd4f35dee356c81d1da380e5d556f77657b82e8cbec3681c27322b",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Reports that IGRAs had sensitivity of 73–83% and specificity of 49–58% for active TB in low- and middle-income countries, so about one in four culture-confirmed patients could test negative. It also notes industry involvement in some of the studies.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44759/blocks/prose-sec-009",
      "source": "sections/sec-009-313-strengths-and-limitations-of-the-evidence-ba.md",
      "source_hash": "a98c9deafc6a5b83bb537474fb7e5c3e128ad4f8b1c2fae5efd4f7def72ce3b8",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes the strengths and limitations of the evidence on IGRAs for active TB, including substantial heterogeneity and the steps taken to reduce it. It also notes the lack of standard definitions of high-incidence settings and of data on patient outcomes or preferences.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44759/blocks/prose-sec-010",
      "source": "sections/sec-010-314-grade-evidence-profiles-and-final-policy-rec.md",
      "source_hash": "90672b072919966a27f55513bd2bad9d56039380227c39cc5d813950bd818d23",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Presents the Expert Group's conclusion that evidence for IGRAs and the skin test in diagnosing active TB was of low quality. It gives the strong recommendation against using them instead of microbiological diagnosis in low- and middle-income countries, given the harm of false positives.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44759/blocks/prose-sec-011",
      "source": "sections/sec-011-32-use-of-igras-in-children.md",
      "source_hash": "750095e825db1ea0024a280e2abc2b44b805c02358655e5549d716f51c14b097",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "A section heading for the use of IGRAs in children.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44759/blocks/prose-sec-012",
      "source": "sections/sec-012-321-study-characteristics.md",
      "source_hash": "f2bde186104d9c87c58523a391e13a9f6655173b734e4a78aba03f8be1d53673",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes the studies on IGRAs in children found through the literature search, covering evaluations in 18 countries. Only a minority came from low- and middle-income countries, and definitions of TB suspects and controls varied.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44759/blocks/prose-sec-013",
      "source": "sections/sec-013-322-summary-of-results.md",
      "source_hash": "d5b595f4370a9fcab9cf87dcd3c78137d9c83e17a6bb0253fe78177732538643",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Reports that most paediatric IGRA studies came from high-income countries, and that in lower-resource settings IGRAs and the skin test showed very similar accuracy for latent and active TB in children. It notes implementation issues such as blood collection and manufacturer support for many studies, mainly through donated kits.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44759/blocks/prose-sec-014",
      "source": "sections/sec-014-323-strengths-and-limitations-of-the-evidence-ba.md",
      "source_hash": "e9417ca76b8d8af93d0670805545bece242c732b031fd7add73204da691c63d4",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes limitations of the paediatric evidence, including very different populations, methods and non-standard reference definitions. Sample sizes were often small, and no data were available on patient outcomes or preferences.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44759/blocks/prose-sec-015",
      "source": "sections/sec-015-324-grade-evidence-profiles-and-final-policy-rec.md",
      "source_hash": "82e0058cbfd28238590f84da3b52302d12e1d61da7c39c1b05aa1581ed49bcfd",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Presents the Expert Group's finding that evidence on IGRAs in children was very low quality. It recommends against using them instead of the skin test for latent or active TB in children in low- and middle-income countries, noting harms of blood collection and unaddressed cost and acceptability.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44759/blocks/prose-sec-016",
      "source": "sections/sec-016-33-use-of-igras-for-the-diagnosis-of-ltbi-in-hiv.md",
      "source_hash": "927a4c9fafb78a575dd978e47b1644b6cf804712b9845d89d25982f9ead7f75e",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "A section heading for the use of IGRAs to diagnose latent TB in people living with HIV.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44759/blocks/prose-sec-017",
      "source": "sections/sec-017-331-study-characteristics.md",
      "source_hash": "996cb0239e98597d0c4bba445a16d97b402de00f693e3eeabcd100ad2dcfd433",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes the studies on IGRAs in immunocompromised people, most from low- and middle-income countries, with wide variation in design and in whether participants with HIV were symptomatic.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44759/blocks/prose-sec-018",
      "source": "sections/sec-018-332-summary-of-results.md",
      "source_hash": "5860bbaa61b21d6e4c305a9d436a6b6821535b128dc9f57b175f66789097fa77",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Reports that the best test for identifying people with HIV who could benefit from isoniazid preventive therapy remains unclear, and that IGRAs and the skin test performed similarly in people with HIV. It notes industry involvement in some studies.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44759/blocks/prose-sec-019",
      "source": "sections/sec-019-333-strengths-and-limitations-of-the-evidence-ba.md",
      "source_hash": "a7f9a8f7f3dd2238cea50b40e8bc7edadd11f805065537f2325866d0d7b23b1c",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes the main limitation of the evidence for people with HIV: no adequate reference standard for latent TB, together with small studies and few head-to-head comparisons.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-44759/blocks/prose-sec-020",
      "source": "sections/sec-020-334-grade-evidence-profiles-and-final-policy-rec.md",
      "source_hash": "aacc94ae2925882e29518d17432e54ad337dac0e6479f0716051ca6f8f4866ec",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Presents the Expert Group's strong recommendation that IGRAs not replace the skin test for latent TB in people living with HIV in low- and middle-income countries, applying also to children with HIV.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
